# Architecture Rules

This project uses a feature-sliced architecture. Follow these rules strictly.

## Directory structure

```
src/
├── app/           → App shell (AuthContext, AppNavigator, providers)
├── features/      → Feature slices, each with screens/, components/, hooks/
├── shared/        → Cross-cutting: components/, lib/, types/
└── services/      → API layer (api.ts) and storage modules (storage/)
```

## Import rules

- Screens import from: `shared/`, `services/`, their own feature's `components/` and `hooks/`
- Features MUST NOT import from other features — extract to `shared/` if needed
- Always import storage via `services/storage` barrel, never from sub-modules directly
- All Supabase edge function calls go through `services/api.ts`

## Adding new features

1. Create `src/features/<name>/screens/<Name>Screen.tsx`
2. Add feature-specific components in `src/features/<name>/components/`
3. Add feature-specific hooks in `src/features/<name>/hooks/`
4. Register the screen in `src/app/AppNavigator.tsx`

## Component placement

- Used by 2+ features → `src/shared/components/`
- Used by 1 feature only → `src/features/<name>/components/`
